{"name":"Bank Vault","hex":"#757374","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bank","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An institution where one can place and borrow money and take care of financial affairs.","A branch office of such an institution."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To deal with a bank or financial institution, or for an institution to provide financial services to a client.","To put into a bank (financial institution)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bank"},{"term":"vault","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An arched masonry structure supporting and forming a ceiling, whether freestanding or forming part of a larger building.","Any arched ceiling or roof."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build as, or cover with a vault.","To store in a vault."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vault"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bank vault","blocks":[{"text":"A bank vault is a secure room used by banks to store and protect valuables, cash, and important documents. Modern bank vaults are typically made of reinforced concrete and steel, with complex locking mechanisms and security systems. This article covers the design, construction, and security features of bank vaults."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/WinonaSavingsBankVault.JPG/330px-WinonaSavingsBankVault.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bank_vault"},{"title":"Bank","blocks":[{"text":"A bank is a financial institution that accepts deposits from the public and creates a demand deposit while making loans. Lending activities can be directly performed by the bank or indirectly through capital markets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/London.bankofengland.arp.jpg/330px-London.bankofengland.arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B